## Context

Child of 0754. The author identified a long initial extraction backlog as a
barrier to useful semantic results. The comparison and pinned implementation
links are in plugins/sdt-sitter/RELEASE-NOTES.md. #6012 searches available
embeddings or uses hybrid lexical fallback while indexing; its attachment
embedding pass follows extraction of the queued attachments. No measured
whole-library duration is asserted.

Read before filing: fork/src/features/search/build.ts and embeddings.ts,
the sitter scheduler and native handoff, and SYNC.md. Upstream catch-up at
357ad1f found new fulltext retry and semantic-mode refusal tests: inspect those
before writing an overlapping probe. Existing target adapters are under
bench/acceptance/; 0754 owns cross-target applicability.

## Work and exit criteria

- [ ] Build a bounded synthetic fixture with distinct metadata-only and
      attachment-content queries, ready packs and a deliberately delayed
      extraction. Observe replies before, during and after indexing.
- [ ] Separate query response latency, time to first useful attachment-content
      semantic result, per-stage coverage over time and eventual completion.
      A metadata or lexical hit must not count as semantic body readiness.
- [ ] Exercise pinned #6012 and the current runnable consumer via existing
      adapters where possible. Record explicit skips when a target cannot
      run; a source reading is not an end-to-end measurement.
- [ ] Compare cold preparation with sitter-prepared current native packs on
      equivalent fresh index states. Verify preparation causes no embedding
      calls and the consumer reuses compatible packs; do not assume its
      installed version has a pack-reading route. Missing integration is a
      named gap, not a simulated passing warm arm.
- [ ] Add controls that hold extraction unresolved and withhold a required
      embedding. Detect search accidentally awaiting the entire build, falsely
      complete coverage and metadata/lexical fallback mislabeled semantic.
      Apply each target's declared behavior and SPEC contract; report a
      difference before prescribing a new fallback policy.
- [ ] Verify that changing chunking/model configuration does not require
      re-extracting compatible current packs where the consumer supports that
      handoff, and that source/processor changes cannot serve falsely current
      downstream content or locations.
- [ ] Commit raw traces with target heads, host, fixtures and phase clocks under
      bench/results/ and a verification/ report cited here; declare quoted
      measurements in bench/check_figures.py.
- [ ] Route demonstrated defects to their current implementation owner.
      Incremental pack consumption, a new scheduler or a new chunk/embedding
      service are design choices, not authorized implementations in this
      measurement ticket. No new latency threshold is invented here.
- [ ] Update 0754's matrix and make check passes.

Use disposable job state under the existing arena lifecycle. Do not launch a
whole-library campaign merely to establish the ordering or readiness behavior.

Reuse the existing conductor-integration and t0028-seg1 fork work, as mapped
in 0754. The runnable assembly and embedding boundary already have owners
(0566, 0554, 0575, with 0565 for segmentation wiring). A missing runnable arm
belongs to those tickets, not a newly invented chunk/embedding sitter.
The indexer/worker rewrite is held per STATE.md; this probe does not lift it.
